{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Do not introduce a new property tax without protecting recent stamp duty payers",
        "additional_details": "Homeowners who recently paid substantial Stamp Duty could be unfairly disadvantaged. They would have paid a large upfront tax under the existing system, only to face a new annual property tax shortly afterwards, while future purchasers benefit from the abolition of Stamp Duty.\r\n\r\nAny reform should provide a full credit for Stamp Duty paid within five years of implementation, applied against future property-tax liabilities, plus a phased transition and protection from excessive increases.",
        "background": "Require any new annual property tax to include a full credit for Stamp Duty paid within the previous five years, with transitional relief for homeowners facing substantial increases.",
